le=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dalu form is for Rituals... What more need be said? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just that the Dalu form is for urban hunts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:39:47-07:00","id":454486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=454483#post454483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just that the Dalu form is for urban hunts.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it has more than a single purpose... that is good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Would be boring if the only reason you took Dalu was for Urban Hunting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:46:45-07:00","id":454502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=453922#post453922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Use the Father's Form for:<ul><li>Reaching things on the top shelf.</li> <li>Pushing stalled vehicles out of traffic.</li> <li>Spotting your packmates on the free weights.</li> <li>Costume contests.</li> <li>Saving seats for your friends at the movies.</li> <li>Rearranging the furniture.</li> <li>Awesome cannonballs at the pool.</li> <li>Finding pants that won't rip when you change shape.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Wild sex in power positions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:54:27-07:00","id":454512,"title":"","content":"I was wondering who'd be the first to point out that they can do that now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:57:29-07:00","id":454517,"title":"","content":"Arcane always brings the kink.<br /> <br /> ....that's a lie. That's a bold-faced lie.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Or would it be more appropriate to say &quot;True story, brah&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-23-2015, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:07:55-07:00","id":454528,"title":"","content":"So yes, I did start this thread with the intention of digging up the tongue in cheek, an I really appreciate those who have run with that. They've been fun and I hope there are more!<br /> <br /> I really like the idea of being able to use Gauru for rituals, too, though. Apparently the writers do too, as that half-page art splat during the discussion of the Facet is of of two Uratha in Gauru performing a ritual around a fire.<br /> Dalu was definitely the rite form in first edition, and still is to a degree (it's on the list of things that give you a bonus to the final rite roll). The nature of both Dalu and rites has changed substantially, though. <br /> While Dalu still causes lunacy if someone notices it, it's possible that you'll just be mistaken for a big dude. The specific power called out on the character sheet is someone in Dalu is a Badass Motherfucker that people will get out of the way of. It has a place in the hunt, and that place is getting the herd away from its group. Because this has always been the case, it also happens to help with all rites.<br /> Rites, very unlike before, are all based on a set of symbols combined into some sort of personalized action. A good handful of rites need symbols of rage and death and claws and blood. Just being in Gauru fulfils three of those and makes the fourth very, very easy. Even to you, Tymeaus, Gauru form is highly meaningful. And it's that meaning that empowers the rites of the People.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T13:54:53-07:00","id":454808,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of a Predator King pack hunting in Gauru. Imagine 12 of those tearing after you in the dark. <br /> <br /> Using it to get to prey, such as through a house, tearing through walls and floorboards. <br /> <br /> I am not a huge fan of the gift, because it seems to open doors for pretty dumb things, but if used as a way to extend the use of Gauru to the final minutes of the hunt, or to chase, such as leaping roof top to roof top. This kind of butts in on Urshal's use, but for a pack trying to horrify prey and harry in a direction, the full lunacy could be useful. <br /> <br /> So basically, final stretch of the hunt, when 20 seconds won't be long enough to finish the job, or when trying to horrify are the main purposes I could see. Otherwise, it's like, chilling with my homeys and I want a claw big enough and a mouth large enough to slam pony kegs in one go because reasons. <br /> <br /> Then again, there is a gift that lets you change genders, which seems kind of unnecessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T14:10:48-07:00","id":454821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=454808#post454808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, there is a gift that lets you change genders, which seems kind of unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Leaving it to Skin Thief is rather tasteless as alternatives go. The children of Father Luna oughtn't need to kill somebody to change their sex. (The word is sex. Gender has nothing to do with your bits.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T14:22:42-07:00","id":454845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=454808#post454808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the full lunacy could be useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your chase ideas. One of the drawbacks of the gift is that you don't get to use full lunacy until you start attacking things or take a fistful of lethal damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T15:08:33-07:00","id":454899,"title":"","content":"In a word? Dance:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SXHxxj1oBeI\" data-code=\"SXHxxj1oBeI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/SXHxxj1oBeI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T15:12:30-07:00","id":454902,"title":"","content":"I approve.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And in fact, I take your Napoleon Dynamite and raise you one Catgroove.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=twqM56f_cVo\" data-code=\"twqM56f_cVo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/twqM56f_cVo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, community theater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-23-2015, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T16:01:14-07:00","id":454970,"title":"","content":"I could see Father's Form being used for either the Blood Talons or the Storm Lords during a gathering. There's ritualistic duels where you must fight each other while wearing the Father's Form, maybe even having it choreographed, but the first one to actually succumb to the rage and actually take on Gauru for real loses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T16:42:40-07:00","id":455019,"title":"","content":"Other than Rituals, I can see that certain spirits might not communicate with you unless you obtain a certain form. Like, for example, there might be a Thirdborn of Huzuruth-Ur out there who will not address his father's get unless they take the form of Urfarah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T16:48:55-07:00","id":455024,"title":"","content":"Assuming the Lord of the Hunt looked like that.<br /> <br /> Somehow, I imagine it's more terrifying still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T16:56:55-07:00","id":455026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455019#post455019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than Rituals, I can see that certain spirits might not communicate with you unless you obtain a certain form. Like, for example, there might be a Thirdborn of Huzuruth-Ur out there who will not address his father's get unless they take the form of Urfarah.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I didn't mean any disrespect.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T17:10:05-07:00","id":455036,"title":"","content":"I always assumed he mostly appeared as a <i>humongous</i> wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T17:13:16-07:00","id":455039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455036#post455036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always assumed he mostly appeared as a <i>humongous</i> wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Mirrors 1e book, he had humanoid children with lupine features. I always thought he could assume anything between the Hishu and Urhan forms of the werewolves, either as a gift from his mate or because he was THAT powerful enough to take many forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T17:13:20-07:00","id":455040,"title":"","content":"It would be useful in some sort of wilderness survival or endurance ordeal. Sun dances are grueling ordeals for humans, and your Storm Lord has so much more to prove than a human. Free-climb Mount Rainier in a winter storm, and stay there a week? I think I have just the ticket.<br /> <br /> OR, you could get your friends together and re-enact New Yorker cartoons, but in Gauru, and post them to your Instagram. No one looks at that anyway, not since hitting Primal-Urge 4 drastically altered the content of your breakfast pics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T17:35:54-07:00","id":455057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455039#post455039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Mirrors 1e book, he had humanoid children with lupine features. I always thought he could assume anything between the Hishu and Urhan forms of the werewolves, either as a gift from his mate or because he was THAT powerful enough to take many forms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Based on Embodiment of the Firstborn and it not specifying there being one form that looks similar to the Firstborn, plus a few sentences and drawings scattered around here or there, I think the Firstborn at least have been known to appear in all five forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-23-2015, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T18:19:13-07:00","id":455101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=454808#post454808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, there is a gift that lets you change genders, which seems kind of unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't find a Facet that gives you a nearly impenetrable disguise, and which can allow you to get into places you normally couldn't without causing a major ruckus useful?<br /> <br /> Like it or not, people categorize people based on a lot of physical factors; one of those is sex. Being able to just be <i>female</i> when the cops are looking for a <i>male</i> suspect is pretty huge. Also, it can be <i>fantastically</i> useful for Iron Masters, depending on what organization they're hunting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T19:35:31-07:00","id":455252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=454528#post454528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rites, very unlike before, are all based on a set of symbols combined into some sort of personalized action. A good handful of rites need symbols of rage and death and claws and blood. Just being in Gauru fulfils three of those and makes the fourth very, very easy. <i><b>Even to you, Tymeaus, Gauru form is highly meaningful</b></i>. And it's that meaning that empowers the rites of the People.</div> </div> </div> </div>You obviously misunderstand my ideas of Gauru form, then. Yes, it is highly meaningful when you absolutely have no other choice and your target must be dead, as long as you do not mind the potential fallout of devastation and death that will surround you if you lose control. It is not a Form I would choose to employ during a Ritual, <i>EVER</i>. If I wanted a more visceral form for a Ritual, it would be Urshul. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 03-23-2015, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T21:02:04-07:00","id":455345,"title":"","content":"I would second tgevpower positions, but so da . None if the NPC's will even go for dalu <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I suppose I'll just have to settle for cuddling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T22:23:04-07:00","id":455442,"title":"","content":"Just because you would not choose it for ritual does NOT mean the spirits wouldn't respect it. I'm not saying you shouldn't have your opinion on the matter, but let's not pretend like it has no place in rituals. The spirits respect the fathers form. The Unihar of 1e were representative of the perfect fathers form. There's lore backing all of this and its importance in the hisil is paramount. <br /> If treating with an ancient spirit of the wilderness can be smoothed by taking the fathers form as a sign of respect? Damn right I'd be doing that. Being able to take the fathers form without succumbing to rage means an incredible amount in the hisil. It proves that you can be something more then a mindless mass of killing fur. Remember in the examples from 2e core. Spirits RESPECT it. They FEAR it. They KNOW it. <br /> <br /> The facet offers so much more then just a furries wet dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T23:43:52-07:00","id":455487,"title":"","content":"All I'll say is that, in all fairness, I'm not thrilled with the Father's Form either. It seems to me mostly just a power statement. It might work in rituals(though I'd argue that there's a reason Dalu is still the rites form), but mostly it's there for any appropriate situation where you need to say &quot;If you throw down, shit <i>will</i> get real&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T23:54:54-07:00","id":455494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455487#post455487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I'll say is that, in all fairness, I'm not thrilled with the Father's Form either. It seems to me mostly just a power statement. It might work in rituals(though I'd argue that there's a reason Dalu is still the rites form), but mostly it's there for any appropriate situation where you need to say &quot;If you throw down, shit <i>will</i> get real&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly I'd just prefer if it was a Merit with a Purity prereq on account of what making it a Facet did to the Pack Gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T00:51:10-07:00","id":455526,"title":"","content":"With this topic I see more in-story usess of Father Form, without bad jokes. Keep it up, guys!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455101#post455101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't find a Facet that gives you a nearly impenetrable disguise, and which can allow you to get into places you normally couldn't without causing a major ruckus useful?<br /> <br /> Like it or not, people categorize people based on a lot of physical factors; one of those is sex. Being able to just be <i>female</i> when the cops are looking for a <i>male</i> suspect is pretty huge. Also, it can be <i>fantastically</i> useful<br /> for Iron Masters, depending on what organization they're hunting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to point to this - as part of LGBT community ( bisexual bear myself ) both this Gift and sidebar about male werewolves becoming pregnant - I'm really glad it's in the 2ed corebook. How is better to show some gender identity questions than Children of Shapeshifting God/des Luna?<br /> <br /> It's equal in importance to me as the Father Form Gift - things that nicely mark weirdness of werewolves race. Even if Father Form I would mark usable only to Rituals, ritual combat or <i>Siskur-Dah</i> ( like last few minutes of Hunt, mentioned before ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T03:08:33-07:00","id":455605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455494#post455494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mostly I'd just prefer if it was a Merit with a Purity prereq on account of what making it a Facet did to the Pack Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>?? Can you elaborate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T03:40:29-07:00","id":455636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455526#post455526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> male werewolves becoming pregnant</div> </div> </div> </div>...Is there a sidebar about this? ...<br /> ...<br /> I never really cared much for Werewolf, but I just realized that I desperately need this book.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:08:04-07:00","id":455833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455442#post455442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because you would not choose it for ritual does NOT mean the spirits wouldn't respect it. I'm not saying you shouldn't have your opinion on the matter, but let's not pretend like it has no place in rituals. The spirits respect the fathers form. The Unihar of 1e were representative of the perfect fathers form. There's lore backing all of this and its importance in the hisil is paramount.<br /> If treating with an ancient spirit of the wilderness can be smoothed by taking the fathers form as a sign of respect? Damn right I'd be doing that. Being able to take the fathers form without succumbing to rage means an incredible amount in the hisil. It proves that you can be something more then a mindless mass of killing fur. Remember in the examples from 2e core. Spirits RESPECT it. They FEAR it. They KNOW it.<br /> <br /> The facet offers so much more then just a furries wet dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Decent Point, except that you are &quot;Cheating&quot; by using a Gift to assume the Father's Form so that you can avoid Rage. Why would something like that garner respect? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now, if you take Gauru Form and risk that rage to show that you have control over it, well, then THAT action garners some respect. Otherwise it is just reminiscent of cWOD's craziness of just being in Garou Form just because you can. I respect the former, and deride the latter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i><b>Satchel's </b></i>Idea is potentially interesting, if he will elaborate a bit on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 03-24-2015, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:22:02-07:00","id":455844,"title":"","content":"How is it cheating, using a facet of a gift that is part of your very being? This is something every uratha can do regardless of allegiance, And potentially from first change might I add.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:37:51-07:00","id":455855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455844#post455844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it cheating, using a facet of a gift that is part of your very being? This is something every uratha can do regardless of allegiance, And potentially from first change might I add.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you are not &quot;Controlling&quot; the Rage at that point, as you claim, you are bypassing it. As I said previously somewhere up above, it smacks too much of cWOD Apocalypse Werewolves, reading poetry whilst sipping wine and debating logic, all in the form that was meant for one thing, and one thing only. There is no &quot;Control&quot; there. If you want to impress with how much Control a werewolf character possesses, take the Gauru Form and then deliver a Speech, all the while making rolls to keep your Rage under control. THAT is control. Having a gift &quot;that anyone can have, at character creation and regardless of allegiance&quot; and then claiming it demonstrates the character's &quot;Control&quot; of the form is disingenuous at best and an outright Lie in the least. That is NOT control. Might as well just bring back unlimited time in Form with no rage issues. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:42:29-07:00","id":455860,"title":"","content":"Just because the player isn't rolling resolve+composure every three seconds doesn't mean the werewolf isn't &quot;controlling&quot; the rage. The Character has <i>learned</i> to suppress it consistently so long as they avoid certain actions. <br /> <br /> You really think a spirit seeing a werewolf sitting there calmly in gauru is going to be less impressed by that than seeing one that can keep it up for a matter of seconds whilst barely holding it together? Ludicrous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:46:34-07:00","id":455861,"title":"","content":"@Tymeaus - All joking aside (and I've very much enjoyed joking about this), the Facet is meant for what you labeled &quot;the former&quot;. There's a price leveled on you for taking Gauru not for combat. It says explicitly in the Facet's description that it's a gift from Urfarah to her children, and one not meant to be taken lightly.<br /> Given your comment above about rites, I think you're missing the point of what rites are supposed to be now. They things you put into them are exactly like your reaction. If Gauru really means to you that someone is going to die, then having Gauru in a ritual cements that as you are performing this rite you mean to evoke claws and rage and death. If Urshul makes you think &quot;I'm strong but in control&quot;, that might not cut it when you need to mean &quot;death&quot; or &quot;rage&quot; by what your actions say in your rite. <br /> I love that Gauru means someone is going down to you. That's totally the right headspace. That sort of headspace is also the one you're supposed to employ when constructing rites.<br /> <br /> As to the Cheating bit, its a Wolf Gift, so it isn't one you had to go find a spirit to help you get. You were born with the capacity to have it, you just had to choose to unlock that Facet of your persona.<br /> <br /> I'm also curious about what Satchel meant about what happened to Pack Gifts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:49:10-07:00","id":455867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455855#post455855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because you are not &quot;Controlling&quot; the Rage at that point, as you claim, you are bypassing it. As I said previously somewhere up above, it smacks too much of cWOD Apocalypse Werewolves, reading poetry whilst sipping wine and debating logic, all in the form that was meant for one thing, and one thing only. There is no &quot;Control&quot; there. If you want to impress with how much Control a werewolf character possesses, take the Gauru Form and then deliver a Speech, all the while making rolls to keep your Rage under control. THAT is control. Having a gift &quot;that anyone can have, at character creation and regardless of allegiance&quot; and then claiming it demonstrates the character's &quot;Control&quot; of the form is disingenuous at best and an outright Lie in the least. That is NOT control. Might as well just bring back unlimited time in Form with no rage issues. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is Chain Rage and Still Small Voice cheating, too, in your opinion? Are elodoth cheaters because they can bypass the rage of other Uratha?<br /> <br /> 'Note the Facet suppresses the need to kill; the desire to kill is still as strong as ever \u2014 bubbling beneath the surface, bound by the silver brands burned into the Uratha\u2019s spirit-self. Like an addiction, the temptation is ever-present and Gauru makes it so very easy to surrender.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:57:06-07:00","id":455879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455861#post455861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Tymeaus - All joking aside (and I've very much enjoyed joking about this), the Facet is meant for what you labeled &quot;the former&quot;. There's a price leveled on you for taking Gauru not for combat. It says explicitly in the Facet's description that it's a gift from Urfarah to her children, and one not meant to be taken lightly.<br /> Given your comment above about rites, I think you're missing the point of what rites are supposed to be now. They things you put into them are exactly like your reaction. If Gauru really means to you that someone is going to die, then having Gauru in a ritual cements that as you are performing this rite you mean to evoke claws and rage and death. If Urshul makes you think &quot;I'm strong but in control&quot;, that might not cut it when you need to mean &quot;death&quot; or &quot;rage&quot; by what your actions say in your rite.<br /> I love that Gauru means someone is going down to you. That's totally the right headspace. That sort of headspace is also the one you're supposed to employ when constructing rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I disagree with you on the Rites part. Again, there is a reason you use Dalu for Rites (and a reason you get benefits for doing so). See, you can kill in Urshul Form just as efficiently as you can in Gauru form (in most cases, in my experience, because you are NOT worrying about the Rage controlling you), with no threat to losing control and killing innocents, should there be any. No worries, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 03-24-2015, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:01:11-07:00","id":455885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455860#post455860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because the player isn't rolling resolve+composure every three seconds doesn't mean the werewolf isn't &quot;controlling&quot; the rage. The Character has <i>learned</i> to suppress it consistently so long as they avoid certain actions.<br /> <br /> You really think a spirit seeing a werewolf sitting there calmly in gauru is going to be less impressed by that than seeing one that can keep it up for a matter of seconds whilst barely holding it together? Ludicrous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then call me ludicrous. I do not see <i><b>P<b>assive</b> </b></i>Gauru forms as being impressive. It leads to such silliness as Gauru Reading Poetry whilst sipping Wine (after all, he is avoiding certain actions, right?) which I find equally ludicrous. Yeah, I know that is way out there, but it is possible, and Player characters often go to ludicrous places because they can. I fall into the portion of the rules that would disallow such shenanigans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:11:44-07:00","id":455889,"title":"","content":"Suppressing the rage through sheer force of will doesn't exactly preclude sipping wine. Hell, do it well enough and there's no visible difference. The spirit would only be able to tell <i>how </i>the uratha was staying calm in gauru if they failed or ran out of time and had to shift back. How is that impressive? It's just reckless and stupid when a much safer alternative is available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:14:45-07:00","id":455897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455879#post455879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, I disagree with you on the Rites part. Again,<b> there is a reason you use Dalu for Rites</b> (and a reason you get benefits for doing so). See, you can kill in Urshul Form just as efficiently as you can in Gauru form (in most cases, in my experience, because you are NOT worrying about the Rage controlling you), with no threat to losing control and killing innocents, should there be any. No worries, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>We're not talking about 1st Ed: Dalu gives no bonuses for performance. Unless you've somehow linked your Dalu form to one of the symbols necessary.<br /> <br /> I get that you don't like 2nd Ed, but don't come into a thread asking about a specific 2nd Ed ability and use 1st Ed conventions.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I am wrong about this. Page 139 has &quot;All participants are in Dalu form&quot; for a +1 modifier. Something I missed on my first few read-throughs. Apologies to Tymeaus Jalynsfein.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":1923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","user":"BigDamnHero","date":". 03-24-2015, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:18:11-07:00","id":455923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455897#post455897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're not talking about 1st Ed: Dalu gives no bonuses for performance. Unless you've somehow linked your Dalu form to one of the symbols necessary.<br /> <br /> I get that you don't like 2nd Ed, but don't come into a thread asking about a specific 2nd Ed ability and use 1st Ed conventions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dalu is the form for the urban hunt in section edition, this is true. But if everyone involved in a ritual is in Dalu form, there is a +1 bonus to completing rites. Some have taken this to mean it is the ritual form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:18:42-07:00","id":455924,"title":"","content":"It gives a bonus if <i>everyone </i>is in dalu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:33:05-07:00","id":455943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455924#post455924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It gives a bonus if <i>everyone </i>is in dalu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh...I was under the same impression as BigDamnHero. Is that rule present in the rites section or the Dalu section?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:34:54-07:00","id":455945,"title":"","content":"Rites. Page 139, top left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:35:25-07:00","id":455947,"title":"","content":"I kinda wonder why that's still in there. I mean, sure, I'm going to make use of it, but I don't know that it makes sense to me.<br /> Is it because you need manual dexterity for most Rites (thereby pre-empting Urhan and Urshul) and they take more than a minute (thereby pre-empting Gauru for most people), thus leaving Dalu and the pretending-to-be-human-still form, giving Dalu more of a ressonance of werewolfhood without making the rituals themselves impossible?<br /> If that's the case, maybe those who can take Gauru during the rite should count towards this bonus. Otherwise it just seems like a holdover from a bygone day. Nothing else about Dalu seems overtly mystical above and beyond the other forms. They can still sort-of hide amongst humans and they have a specific purpose in all hunts which is not &quot;start it and make it sacred.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:47:12-07:00","id":455957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455605#post455605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ?? Can you elaborate?</div> </div> </div> </div>It takes up the Purity Facet slot in the Gift of Change, which appears to have pushed Maw of Madness over to the Gift of Pack, which a couple of people have remarked is a tad unsuited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:56:34-07:00","id":455971,"title":"","content":"I wanna get back to silliness that was asked for by Ben, so while y'all are going on about this, I just want to leave you the image of a Gauru going grocery shopping, a little basket held in the crook of their arm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T10:28:42-07:00","id":455990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455971#post455971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanna get back to silliness that was asked for by Ben, so while y'all are going on about this, I just want to leave you the image of a Gauru going grocery shopping, a little basket held in the crook of their arm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even better: a little old lady Gauru in a knitted sweater, an old skirt and dainty little shoes that the massive Gauru paws just barely fit in. Put a pair of glasses on for extra points.<br /> <br /> &quot;Grandma, what big ears you have!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;All the better to hear misbehaving children outside, my pup.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;And Grandma, what big teeth you have!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh honey, this is just so I don't get mugged in the Wal-Mart parking lot. When was the last time you saw one of these hoodlums point a knife at pearly whites like these?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T11:02:15-07:00","id":456003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=455947#post455947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda wonder why that's still in there. I mean, sure, I'm going to make use of it, but I don't know that it makes sense to me.<br /> Is it because you need manual dexterity for most Rites (thereby pre-empting Urhan and Urshul) and they take more than a minute (thereby pre-empting Gauru for most people), thus leaving Dalu and the pretending-to-be-human-still form, giving Dalu more of a ressonance of werewolfhood without making the rituals themselves impossible?<br /> If that's the case, maybe those who can take Gauru during the rite should count towards this bonus. Otherwise it just seems like a holdover from a bygone day. <i><b>Nothing else about Dalu seems overtly mystical above and beyond the other forms</b></i>. They can still sort-of hide amongst humans and they have a specific purpose in all hunts which is not &quot;start it and make it sacred.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I would reply that the Gauru form is also not overtly mystical, so why would it have more weight? The fact that there is a bonus to Dalu seems to me to show that it <i><b>is </b></i>the Form for Rites. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T11:20:55-07:00","id":456025,"title":"","content":"There's only a bonus to Dalu if everyone is in that form. If one person is not in Dalu form, there is no bonus from it. It likely doesn't mention Gauru form offering a bonus because using Gauru form for other than killing is dependent upon a gift. <br /> <br /> 'Some lodges insist their members learn how to control themselves in Gauru because of the sacred connotations it holds. They practice rituals and ceremonies in Gauru that they believe bring enlightenment. Even if not strictly true, these practices foster closer bonds between lodge members. Furthermore, the Gauru form is a powerful and undeniable symbol of the essence of the werewolf, and many ritemasters use it for their rites. Uratha who embrace Gauru for ritual purposes tend to hold a dim view of werewolves who profane the sacred form, and have no time for those who only use Gauru for fighting and killing.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T11:36:15-07:00","id":456039,"title":"","content":"There's also the fact that being in Gauru form is an implicit threat. It's like carrying a bazooka with you everywhere.<br /> <br /> Just because you're having a tea-party with your bazooka doesn't mean that you <i>don't have a fracking bazooka</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T12:01:24-07:00","id":456084,"title":"","content":"I suppose it would be weird given the tenor of the conversation to mention that in the Tokyo setting I'm fiddling around with there's a vampire elder with a werewolf lover who has The Father's Form.<br /> <br /> Their bedroom activities involve it. It's all the jaded vampire's fault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T12:04:58-07:00","id":456088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=456084#post456084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it would be weird given the tenor of the conversation to mention that in the Tokyo setting I'm fiddling around with there's a vampire elder with a werewolf lover who has The Father's Form.<br /> <br /> Their bedroom activities involve it. It's all the jaded vampire's fault.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all his fault she now likes bedroom activities that would kill mortal women.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T12:05:19-07:00","id":456089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=456084#post456084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it would be weird given the tenor of the conversation to mention that in the Tokyo setting I'm fiddling around with there's a vampire elder with a werewolf lover who has The Father's Form.<br /> <br /> Their bedroom activities involve it. It's all the jaded vampire's fault.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems fine, though I could see the drinking might endangering it. I tend to portray Werewolf blood as very satisfying.<br /> <br /> And because I don't think anyone will really care much if the argument gets derailed, does anyone think a werewolf with Cunning 5 could use Cold Embrace to impersonate a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T12:11:42-07:00","id":456096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=456089#post456089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems fine, though I could see the drinking might endangering it. I tend to portray Werewolf blood as very satisfying.<br /> <br /> And because I don't think anyone will really care much if the argument gets derailed, does anyone think a werewolf with Cunning 5 could use Cold Embrace to impersonate a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They tend to do the blood drinking in forms other than the Father's Form before or after the other activities.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah; I could see Cold Embrace working at that level.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T12:33:54-07:00","id":456130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=456039#post456039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the fact that being in Gauru form is an implicit threat. It's like carrying a bazooka with you everywhere.<br /> <br /> Just because you're having a tea-party with your bazooka doesn't mean that you <i>don't have a fracking bazooka</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better yet, have a tea party WITH the Father's Form for all members involved, AND equip everyone with a bazooka. Room service is probably fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T12:37:00-07:00","id":456131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=456084#post456084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it would be weird given the tenor of the conversation to mention that in the Tokyo setting I'm fiddling around with there's a vampire elder with a werewolf lover who has The Father's Form.<br /> <br /> Their bedroom activities involve it. It's all the jaded vampire's fault.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually find that kind of sweet, in it's own weird way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T12:43:52-07:00","id":456141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=456131#post456131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually find that kind of sweet, in it's own weird way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because lesser forms seem inadequate to share in such a moment with their lover?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T12:55:51-07:00","id":456155,"title":"","content":"It just might be flashbacks to Wolf Children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T12:57:14-07:00","id":456157,"title":"","content":"I imagine the Father's Form being used at some kind of big gathering, like a moot of all the local Packs or a Protectorate, especially if there are Wolf-blooded or others in attendance. All forms are the true form of the Uratha, but I do like the power statement and how clear it makes it to others that they are not just wolves or men.<br /> <br /> While I know that Rage isn't actually seen as a bad thing, I do think one could also look at the Father's Form as a status symbol for how in-control those who can wear it are. The idea I got from it was that you've learned through the gift to suppress your crazy death rage when you take the form, rather than you taking a form where the death rage is less severe. In that way, it reads like a symbol of willpower.<br /> <br /> When it comes down to it, it feels cosmetic, but I'm a big fan of cosmetics, so that's cool with me. Admittedly, I'm a bit less jazzed with the whole furry connection that some people assign to Apocalypse, and that they might consequently assign to this Facet, but different strokes for different folks. Big scary wolfpeople are pretty cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T13:05:04-07:00","id":456158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=456155#post456155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just might be flashbacks to Wolf Children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, so you saw that movie too. I have it on DVD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T13:10:26-07:00","id":456161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=456157#post456157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes down to it, it feels cosmetic, but I'm a big fan of cosmetics, so that's cool with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been my thought about a lot of the Wolf Gifts, which is a large part of why I support the 1XP version of them from the quick-guide chart rather than the 2XP version from the text.<br /> <br /> This is a game about storytelling, though, so in a way cosmetics are everything...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T13:23:26-07:00","id":456173,"title":"","content":"Wolf children is one of the saddest films I've seen. <br /> <br /> As for the form, I'd rule staying in gauru adds intimidation rolls vs spirits. How do they know it's a gift and you aren't just primal urge 50?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T13:25:38-07:00","id":456174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=456089#post456089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And because I don't think anyone will really care much if the argument gets derailed, does anyone think a werewolf with Cunning 5 could use Cold Embrace to impersonate a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cunning 5 will let you go a long way towards impersonating a vampire, yes. I <i>think</i> that the Requiem predatory aura rules mess with the ability to totally get away with being a Kindred in speciifc but I'm not entirely sure.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T16:07:20-07:00","id":456295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453432-what-would-you-do-with-the-father-s-form?p=456155#post456155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just might be flashbacks to Wolf Children.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love that movie. Speaking of which, maybe that's a possible consequence of father's form related sexiness. If any children conceived in the act go through the First Change, it happens when they are unusually young.<br /> <br /> Of course, in addition to Wolf Children, I've been reading some of Linda Godfry's cryptozoology books on alleged werewolf sightings in the US and one sighting is of a mother werewolf and her three puppies, all in Gauru, crossing the road in front of the witness. So the idea of werewolves using Gauru for non killing related stuff is okay with me and so is the idea of werewolf puppies in Gauru.<br /> <br /> And not to derail, but, I would recommend Godfry's work for any ST in need of story seeds. Just take a sighting from her books and try to figure out what the werewolf/wolves in the sighting were up to.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a h